{
  "about": [
    "Where Muse's finds come from, for each area of the topic map. `npm run record:media` reads the newest items of every source here, keeps the ones whose links answer, files each under topics, and writes server/fixtures/media.json.",
    "articles: RSS or Atom feeds of magazines, museums and blogs. youtube: channel handles (their videos and Shorts are read from the channel pages). vimeo: channel or user feeds. flickr: tag sets (every tag must match). bluesky: account handles. instagram: public business or creator accounts, read only when META_IG_TOKEN is set.",
    "search: a word that keeps a topic search in the area (\"Ultramarine\" plus \"pigment\"). A topic the sources above leave with fewer than 3 items is filled from Bluesky posts that name it.",
    "Edit freely: add or remove entries, then re-record. A source that stops answering is reported and skipped."
  ],
